// Unused-export gate. Run via `pnpm unused-exports-gate`.
//
// **There is no `paths` map, and that is a measurement rather than an omission.**
//
// This file used to carry one, mapping each `@kerdial/*` specifier to its
// source entry, on the stated grounds that `package.json` `main` points at a
// gitignored `dist/` so knip could not otherwise follow a re-export chain like
// `api -> market-composition -> market-ingestion`. The header recorded that as
// red-confirmed against `onDemandQuoteRefreshBucket`.
//
// It did not reproduce. Removing the map — the whole map, not one entry —
// changes nothing that can be measured:
//
//   * with the map gone and a deliberately dead export added to
//     `market/ingestion`, the gate still reports it and still exits 1;
//   * with the map gone and no dead export, the gate reports no unused export
//     anywhere and exits 0 — so removing it introduces no false positive;
//   * both of the above hold with **every `dist/` deleted**, which is the
//     precise scenario the old header said the map existed for.
//
// That last probe is the one that settles it. If knip were resolving these
// specifiers through `main: ./dist/index.js`, deleting `dist/` would break the
// resolution and the chain-consumed exports would light up as unused. They do
// not, so knip is not reading `main` at all: it resolves a workspace package to
// its workspace and uses the `entry` configured below.
//
// `onDemandQuoteRefreshBucket` — the export the old claim named — is still the
// live case: defined in `market/ingestion/src/quote-refresh.ts`, re-exported by
// `market/composition/src/index.ts`, consumed by `api`. It is not flagged, with
// or without a `paths` map.
//
// The gate covers the six originally over-exporting packages plus `ledger`;
// widening it to web/api/tools is a separate decision (their entry surfaces are
// shaped differently).
//
// **`ledger`'s entry is configured and the gate still cannot see most of it
// (measured).** `ledger/src/index.ts` re-exports through 17 `export * from`
// lines, and knip does not attribute individual names through a star re-export:
// a deliberately dead export added to `instrument-provider-map-service.ts` is
// **not** reported while that module is star-exported, and **is** reported the
// moment the same line is written as a named re-export. So this entry gates
// `ledger`'s internal modules and not its public surface.
//
// A second measurement from the same probe, which matters more: knip counts a
// workspace's own test files as consumers, so the five caller-less re-mapping
// functions that prompted adding `ledger` were **never** going to be flagged — their unit
// test imports them. Adding `ledger` here would not have caught them. Both
// findings are tracked separately; the entry stays because it is correct and
// becomes load-bearing the moment the star re-exports go.
//
// **Both were decided on 2026-09-07, and the answers live in
// `scripts/unused-exports-gate.ts` — read its header before changing anything
// here.** In short:
//
//   * the star re-exports **stay** (converting them trades a known blindness
//     for the by-value drift this file has three recorded instances of), and
//     the gate now pins their count per workspace, so a new `export * from`
//     in a gated entry fails and the numbers can only be lowered;
//   * test files **should not** count as consumers, and `knip --production`
//     cannot express that here — measured, per-workspace it reports 92 false
//     positives (it cannot see cross-workspace consumers) and whole-repo it
//     reports 438 (only 8 of ~20 workspaces have an `entry` configured). So
//     `unused-exports-gate` finds exports nothing at all imports, **not**
//     exports only tests import. Closing that gap needs the widening deferred
//     three paragraphs above, not a flag.
{
  "include": ["exports", "types"],
  "includeEntryExports": true,
  "workspaces": {
    ".": {
      "entry": ["vitest.global-setup.ts", "scripts/*.ts", "eslint.config.mjs"],
      "project": [],
    },
    "market/ingestion": {
      "entry": ["src/index.ts"],
      "project": "src/**/*.ts",
    },
    "market/composition": {
      "entry": ["src/index.ts", "src/worker-main.ts"],
      "project": "src/**/*.ts",
    },
    "market/ports": {
      "entry": ["src/index.ts"],
      "project": "src/**/*.ts",
    },
    "valuation": {
      "entry": ["src/index.ts"],
      "project": "src/**/*.ts",
    },
    "platform/auth": {
      "entry": ["src/index.ts"],
      "project": "src/**/*.ts",
    },
    // csv-import CI-5. New package, wired in from day one so
    // the gate is never retro-fitted onto an already-over-exporting surface.
    "ledger": {
      "entry": ["src/index.ts"],
      "project": "src/**/*.ts",
    },
    "importer": {
      "entry": ["src/index.ts"],
      "project": "src/**/*.ts",
    },
  },
}
